    "raw": "{\"ruleId\":\"item-0d947a0050a9\",\"class\":\"partial\",\"constraints\":[{\"id\":\"git-push-force-single-line\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\bgit\\\\s+push\\\\b[^;|&]*(-f\\\\b|--force\\\\b)\",\"path\":\".floor/command.txt\"}],\"coverage\":\"Every match of the rule's regex that lies on one line of the command text. The command is lower-cased first, matching the i flag. Each such match makes the check fail.\",\"residual\":\"Is this a bash or powershell tool call whose command text, within its first 8192 characters, matches the regex only when the match crosses a line break, for example `git push` on one line and `-f` on a later line with no `;`, `|` or `&` between them?\",\"probes\":{\"violating\":[{\"tool_name\":\"Bash\",\"tool_input\":{\"command\":\"git push origin main --force\"}},{\"tool_name\":\"Bash\",\"tool_input\":{\"command\":\"cd repo && git push -f origin feature\"}}],\"compliant\":{\"tool_name\":\"Bash\",\"tool_input\":{\"command\":\"git push origin main; rm -f tmp.txt\"}}},\"rationale\":\"The checker matches one line at a time, but the rule's [^;|&]* and \\\\s+ can match across newlines. So matches spanning lines in multi-line commands are missed. The checker also cannot apply the 8192-character limit or the bash/powershell restriction: command.txt is filled for any tool that has a string command field. The usual single-line forced pushes are decided exactly.\"}",
